before:
```react
function App() {
  const [open, setOpen] = React.useState(false);
  return <main>
    <button aria-expanded={open} aria-controls="detail" onClick={() => setOpen(value => !value)}>Details</button>
    {open ? <section id="detail"><h2>Trail notes</h2><p>Bring a pencil.</p></section> : null}
  </main>;
}
```
Initially only Details appears. One click creates the section; another removes it.

```react
function App() {
  const [open, setOpen] = React.useState(true);
  return <main>
    <button aria-expanded={open} aria-controls="detail" onClick={() => setOpen(value => !value)}>Details</button>
    {open ? <section id="detail"><h2>Trail notes</h2><p>Bring a pencil.</p></section> : null}
  </main>;
}
```
This changed App starts open because its initial value is true. Its first click removes the panel.

after:
```react
function App() {
  const [open, setOpen] = React.useState(false);
  return (
    <main>
      <button
        aria-expanded={open}
        aria-controls="detail"
        onClick={() => setOpen(value => !value)}
      >Details</button>
      {open ? (
        <section id="detail">
          <h2>Trail notes</h2>
          <p>Bring a pencil.</p>
        </section>
      ) : null}
    </main>
  );
}
```
The panel starts closed. One click adds the section. Another removes it.
